export default {"format":"cadcraft-help","version":1,"app":"bimcraft","addon":"twin","name":"Digital twin","sections":{"start":"Getting started","tasks":"Walkthroughs","switching":"Coming from other software","reference":"Reference","trouble":"Troubleshooting and limits"},"topics":[{"slug":"digital-twin","scope":"addon:twin","title":"Digital twin: run a plant layout inside your building","summary":"Put a Material flow cell or layout file on a level, see the equipment in the 3D view, check it against the walls, and run the flow and a soft PLC on it.","section":"tasks","order":20,"keywords":["digital twin","material flow","conveyor","plc","layout","throughput","commissioning","walls","fit"],"headings":[{"id":"put-a-layout-in-your-building","text":"Put a layout in your building","level":2},{"id":"what-the-building-gives-and-what-it-does-not","text":"What the building gives, and what it does not","level":2}],"html":"\u003Ch2 id=\"put-a-layout-in-your-building\"\u003EPut a layout in your building\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESwitch on the \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EDigital twin\u003C/span\u003E add-on and open its tab in the right panel.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUnder \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EStart from a cell\u003C/span\u003E choose a ready cell and press \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EUse this cell\u003C/span\u003E, or press \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EOpen a layout file\u003C/span\u003E to load one made in Material flow (ModelCraft). The layout is kept in your IFC file, so saving the model saves it, and Undo takes it back.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EChoose the \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ELevel\u003C/span\u003E it stands on, its X and Y in millimetres and its turn. The equipment is drawn in the 3D view there.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECheck against the walls\u003C/span\u003E puts every box of the equipment against the level&#039;s walls, in plan and in height, and names the items that touch one.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe rest of the panel is the same as in ModelCraft: show a run, test the controls with a soft PLC and faults, compare layouts, read a measured line, and get a bill of materials.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"what-the-building-gives-and-what-it-does-not\"\u003EWhat the building gives, and what it does not\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA building model carries rooms, walls and levels. It does not carry how machines behave, so the speeds, times and logic are the ones in the layout and the panel. The check looks only at the equipment&#039;s boxes against walls: doors and windows are not looked at, and the flow run does not know about the walls. Putting a run into the model&#039;s timeline and saving a video are not offered in BimCraft. Nothing here is a safety validation.\u003C/p\u003E","text":"Put a layout in your building Switch on the Digital twin add-on and open its tab in the right panel. Under Start from a cell choose a ready cell and press Use this cell, or press Open a layout file to load one made in Material flow (ModelCraft). The layout is kept in your IFC file, so saving the model saves it, and Undo takes it back. Choose the Level it stands on, its X and Y in millimetres and its turn. The equipment is drawn in the 3D view there. Check against the walls puts every box of the equipment against the level's walls, in plan and in height, and names the items that touch one. The rest of the panel is the same as in ModelCraft: show a run, test the controls with a soft PLC and faults, compare layouts, read a measured line, and get a bill of materials. What the building gives, and what it does not A building model carries rooms, walls and levels. It does not carry how machines behave, so the speeds, times and logic are the ones in the layout and the panel. The check looks only at the equipment's boxes against walls: doors and windows are not looked at, and the flow run does not know about the walls. Putting a run into the model's timeline and saving a video are not offered in BimCraft. Nothing here is a safety validation."}]};
